-- int-tests-consistency: the cross-group consistency register, part 2: the questions that two or more groups answered, run on the same facts.
-- Each section states the question, what each group did, and then asserts it. EXPECTED VALUES were decided by hand from the Law and from each group's declared reading before the module was run.
--   (A) IP33, the meaning of "year": groups G3 (Article 8(3)(j)) and G5 (Article 13(7)) must take ONE reading.
--   (B) IP35, the unit of a term of imprisonment: groups G6, G7, G8 and G9 must take ONE unit, and on the days reading the four are NOT consistent with one another about "2 years" (see the last assertions).
--   (C) What "a registered charity" is: group G1 (Article 1) requires an entity within Article 2(1); groups G4 (Article 12(7)) and G8 (Article 26(2)) read the standing on the register alone.
--   (D) "Minister" (traps T3, T4): group G1 gives the office text by text (IP3); group G2 reads a Minister generically (reading taken) or as the defined term (the other reading, with IP3).
--   (E) Inclusive and exclusive limits ("not more than", "at least", "more than"), at the boundary, in groups G6 and G9.

§ `Integration layer -- consistency register: year, unit, registered charity, Minister, limits`

GIVETH A `Readings of the fleet`
fleet MEANS `Int the favoured readings of the fleet`

§§ `(A) IP33 -- one reading of "year" for the annual return`

GIVETH A `Readings of the fleet`
`the readings with the charity's own financial year` MEANS `Int the readings of the fleet` `the charity's own financial year` `calendar months`
-- Setting the year once sets it in both groups; a record built by hand with the two fields apart is not consistent.
#ASSERT `Int the readings of the fleet are consistent` `the readings with the charity's own financial year`
#ASSERT ((`the readings with the charity's own financial year`)'s `reading of Articles 8 to 10`)'s `meaning of the year of an annual return` EQUALS `the charity's own financial year`
#ASSERT ((`the readings with the charity's own financial year`)'s `reading of Articles 13 and 14`)'s `the meaning of the year of an annual return` EQUALS `the charity's own financial year`
GIVETH A `Readings of the fleet`
`readings in which G3 and G5 disagree on the year` MEANS
    `Readings of the fleet` WITH
        `reading of Articles 1 and 2` IS (fleet's `reading of Articles 1 and 2`)
        `reading of Articles 3 to 7` IS (fleet's `reading of Articles 3 to 7`)
        `reading of Articles 8 to 10` IS ((`the readings with the charity's own financial year`)'s `reading of Articles 8 to 10`)
        `reading of Articles 11 and 12` IS (fleet's `reading of Articles 11 and 12`)
        `reading of Articles 13 and 14` IS (fleet's `reading of Articles 13 and 14`)
        `reading of Articles 15 to 20` IS (fleet's `reading of Articles 15 to 20`)
        `reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes` IS (fleet's `reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`)
        `reading of Articles 26 to 36` IS (fleet's `reading of Articles 26 to 36`)
        `reading of Schedules 1 and 2` IS (fleet's `reading of Schedules 1 and 2`)
        `meaning of the year of an annual return` IS `the calendar year`
        `unit of a term of imprisonment` IS `calendar months`
#ASSERT NOT `Int the readings of the fleet are consistent` `readings in which G3 and G5 disagree on the year`
-- On the same facts the two groups' years end on the same day. A charity with a 30 June year end, asked on 1 February 2027: G3's most recent year (financial reading) is the year to 30 June 2026,
-- and G5's year containing 1 December 2026 (financial reading) is 1 July 2026 to 30 June 2027; the return for the year to 30 June 2026 (sent 1 September 2026) is G3's "sent for the most recent year".
-- Under the calendar reading the same return does not count: the most recent year is 2026 (ended 31 December 2026) and no return for it has been sent.
GIVETH A `Facts for the annual return entry (Article 8(3)(j))`
`facts of a charity with a 30 June year end that sent its return for the year to 30 June 2026` MEANS
    `Facts for the annual return entry (Article 8(3)(j))` WITH
        `a date on which the charity's financial year ends` IS JUST (YMD 2026 6 30)
        `annual returns sent` IS LIST (`Annual return sent by a charity (Article 8(3)(j))` WITH `last day of the year to which it relates` IS YMD 2026 6 30, `date sent` IS YMD 2026 9 1)
#ASSERT `Art 8(3)(j) the registered charity has sent its annual return for the most recent year` ((`the readings with the charity's own financial year`)'s `reading of Articles 8 to 10`) `the school company as the register holds it` (YMD 2027 2 1) `facts of a charity with a 30 June year end that sent its return for the year to 30 June 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 8(3)(j) the registered charity has sent its annual return for the most recent year` ((fleet)'s `reading of Articles 8 to 10`) `the school company as the register holds it` (YMD 2027 2 1) `facts of a charity with a 30 June year end that sent its return for the year to 30 June 2026`

GIVETH A `Registered charity`
`the school company as the register holds it` MEANS
    `Int IP7 the registered charity` fleet (`Int IP5 the entity` fleet `the text of 2 October 2026` EMPTY (YMD 2026 10 2) `Int fx the registered school company`) `Int fx the register entry of the school company`

§§ `(B) IP35 -- one unit for a term of imprisonment; on the days reading "2 years" is 730 days in three groups and 24 calendar months in the fourth`

GIVETH A `Readings of the fleet`
`the readings with the days unit` MEANS `Int the readings of the fleet` `the calendar year` `days`
#ASSERT `Int the readings of the fleet are consistent` `the readings with the days unit`
-- Calendar months (the reading taken by all four): a sentence of 2 years from 2 October 2026 ends 2 October 2028, 731 days later (2028 has 29 February). G6 (Article 20(6)), G7 (Articles 21(9), 23(7)) and G8 (Article 26(10), 29(1))
-- accept up to 731 days; G9's cap (Schedule 2 paragraph 4(3)(f)) accepts a penalty of 24 months from that day.
#ASSERT `Art 20(6) a term of days from the start is within the maximum of two years` ((fleet)'s `reading of Articles 15 to 20`) (YMD 2026 10 2) 731
#ASSERT NOT `Art 20(6) a term of days from the start is within the maximum of two years` ((fleet)'s `reading of Articles 15 to 20`) (YMD 2026 10 2) 732
#ASSERT `Art 21(9) and 23(7) a sentence of a number of days beginning on a day is within the maximum` 731 (YMD 2026 10 2) ((fleet)'s `reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 21(9) and 23(7) a sentence of a number of days beginning on a day is within the maximum` 732 (YMD 2026 10 2) ((fleet)'s `reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`)
#ASSERT `Art 26 and 29 a term of imprisonment is within the maximum` ((fleet)'s `reading of Articles 26 to 36`) `the offence of providing false information under Article 26(10)` (YMD 2026 10 2) 731
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4(3)(f) the penalty is within the cap` ((fleet)'s `reading of Schedules 1 and 2`) `24 months and a fine` (YMD 2026 10 2)
-- Days (the other reading, set once for all four): G6, G7 and G8 take 2 years as 730 days.
#ASSERT `Art 20(6) a term of days from the start is within the maximum of two years` ((`the readings with the days unit`)'s `reading of Articles 15 to 20`) (YMD 2026 10 2) 730
#ASSERT NOT `Art 20(6) a term of days from the start is within the maximum of two years` ((`the readings with the days unit`)'s `reading of Articles 15 to 20`) (YMD 2026 10 2) 731
#ASSERT `Art 21(9) and 23(7) a sentence of a number of days beginning on a day is within the maximum` 730 (YMD 2026 10 2) ((`the readings with the days unit`)'s `reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 21(9) and 23(7) a sentence of a number of days beginning on a day is within the maximum` 731 (YMD 2026 10 2) ((`the readings with the days unit`)'s `reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`)
#ASSERT `Art 26 and 29 a term of imprisonment is within the maximum` ((`the readings with the days unit`)'s `reading of Articles 26 to 36`) `the offence of providing false information under Article 26(10)` (YMD 2026 10 2) 730
#ASSERT NOT `Art 26 and 29 a term of imprisonment is within the maximum` ((`the readings with the days unit`)'s `reading of Articles 26 to 36`) `the offence of providing false information under Article 26(10)` (YMD 2026 10 2) 731
-- ...but G9's cap still reads the 24 months stored in the `Penalty provided` of the offence (that record stores months on either unit), converts them to days FROM THE DAY the term would run, and compares with 730:
-- 24 months from 2 October 2026 is 731 days (29 February 2028 lies inside), so the very penalty G7, G8 and G6 treat as the maximum "2 years" is OVER the cap of the same 2 years. From 2 October 2025 (no 29 February inside) it is 730 and within.
-- This is a seam found by running all four groups on one unit; it does not arise on calendar months.
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 4(3)(f) the penalty is within the cap` ((`the readings with the days unit`)'s `reading of Schedules 1 and 2`) `24 months and a fine` (YMD 2026 10 2)
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4(3)(f) the penalty is within the cap` ((`the readings with the days unit`)'s `reading of Schedules 1 and 2`) `24 months and a fine` (YMD 2025 10 2)

GIVETH A `Penalty provided`
`24 months and a fine` MEANS
    `Penalty provided` WITH `imprisonment up to, in months` IS JUST 24, fine IS `a fine with no maximum stated in the Law`

§§ `(C) "a registered charity": G1 requires an entity within Article 2(1); G4 (12(7)) and G8 (26(2)) read the standing alone`

-- An NPO body corporate entered in the general section but asked about in the text of 15 October 2025, which has no sub-paragraph (ba): it falls within no sub-paragraph of Article 2(1), so it is not an
-- "entity" and (G1) not a registered charity, though the register records it in the general section.
GIVETH A `Body in the case`
`the NPO body corporate entered in the general section` MEANS
    `Body in the case` WITH
        name IS "Les Amis du Jardin"
        standing IS `entered in the general section`
        purposes IS (`Int fx the registered school company`)'s purposes
        facts IS `Int fx an NPO body corporate`
        model IS `Int fx clear model facts`
        people IS LIST (`Int fx a director with nothing to report called` "M. Du Feu")

GIVETH AN Entity
`that body as Article 2 leaves it in the text of 12 April 2023` MEANS
    `Int IP5 the entity` fleet `the text of 12 April 2023` EMPTY (YMD 2025 10 15) `the NPO body corporate entered in the general section`
GIVETH AN Entity
`that body as Article 2 leaves it in the text of 16 October 2025` MEANS
    `Int IP5 the entity` fleet `the text of 16 October 2025` EMPTY (YMD 2025 10 16) `the NPO body corporate entered in the general section`

#ASSERT (`that body as Article 2 leaves it in the text of 12 April 2023`)'s `kinds of entity` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT `Int IP6 the entity is a registered charity` `that body as Article 2 leaves it in the text of 12 April 2023`
#ASSERT `Int IP6 the entity is a registered charity` `that body as Article 2 leaves it in the text of 16 October 2025`
-- G8 Article 26(2): the entity itself, in the general section, is a person who may be required to provide information, whatever the text says about its kind (the standing alone decides).
GIVETH A `Person addressed by a notice under Article 26`
`the NPO body corporate itself as the person addressed` MEANS
    `Person addressed by a notice under Article 26` WITH `capacity of the person under Article 26(2)` IS `the entity itself`, `standing of the entity on the register` IS `entered in the general section`, `the entity was formerly a registered charity` IS FALSE, `governor while the entity was registered` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 26(2) the person falls within Article 26(2)` ((fleet)'s `reading of Articles 26 to 36`) `the NPO body corporate itself as the person addressed`

§§ `(D) "Minister": the office is the defined term (IP3, group G1); group G2 reads "a Minister" generically (taken) or as the defined term (F2.3 reading B)`

-- A constitution expressly permits the Minister for External Relations to control the entity's activities, in that capacity. Reading taken (any Minister of the Government of Jersey): the bar of Article 5(2) applies in every text.
-- Reading B (only the Minister as Article 1 defines it): the bar applies where that office is the one the definition names in the text. In the text of 12 April 2023 that is the Chief Minister, so the bar does not apply to the Minister for External
-- Relations; in the text of 16 October 2025 it is the Minister for External Relations, so it does.
GIVETH A `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)`
`a constitution permitting the Minister for External Relations to control the entity` MEANS
    `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)` WITH `permissions that the constitution expressly makes` IS LIST (`Permission that a constitution expressly makes` WITH `what the constitution expressly permits` IS `the activities of the entity to be directed or otherwise controlled by`, `the person permitted` IS `a Minister` (JUST `the Minister for External Relations`), `acting in that capacity` IS TRUE)
GIVETH A `Readings of the fleet`
`the readings with F2.3 read as B` MEANS `Int fx the readings with the reading of Articles 3 to 7` fleet `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.3 read as B`
#ASSERT `Art 5(2) the constitution defeats the charity test` ((fleet)'s `reading of Articles 3 to 7`) (`Int IP3 the office of the Minister` `the text of 12 April 2023`) `a constitution permitting the Minister for External Relations to control the entity`
#ASSERT `Art 5(2) the constitution defeats the charity test` ((fleet)'s `reading of Articles 3 to 7`) (`Int IP3 the office of the Minister` `the text of 16 October 2025`) `a constitution permitting the Minister for External Relations to control the entity`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 5(2) the constitution defeats the charity test` ((`the readings with F2.3 read as B`)'s `reading of Articles 3 to 7`) (`Int IP3 the office of the Minister` `the text of 12 April 2023`) `a constitution permitting the Minister for External Relations to control the entity`
#ASSERT `Art 5(2) the constitution defeats the charity test` ((`the readings with F2.3 read as B`)'s `reading of Articles 3 to 7`) (`Int IP3 the office of the Minister` `the text of 16 October 2025`) `a constitution permitting the Minister for External Relations to control the entity`

§§ `(E) inclusive and exclusive limits at the boundary`

-- Article 20(5): a disqualification order for a period "not exceeding 15 years": an order beginning 1 March 2026 may end on 1 March 2041 (the anniversary; F6.14, reading taken) and not on 2 March 2041.
GIVEN end IS A DATE @desc The last day of the order
GIVETH A `Disqualification order`
`a disqualification order from 1 March 2026 to` end MEANS
    `Disqualification order` WITH person IS "A. Le Brun", `begins on` IS YMD 2026 3 1, `last day of the period` IS end
#ASSERT `Art 20(5) the order's period is within the limit` ((fleet)'s `reading of Articles 15 to 20`) (`a disqualification order from 1 March 2026 to` (YMD 2041 3 1))
#ASSERT NOT `Art 20(5) the order's period is within the limit` ((fleet)'s `reading of Articles 15 to 20`) (`a disqualification order from 1 March 2026 to` (YMD 2041 3 2))
-- Schedule 2 paragraph 1(1): at least 4 and not more than 8 members of the tribunal: 4 and 8 are inside the limits; 3 and 9 are outside.
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 1(1) the number of members of the tribunal is within the limits` 4
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 1(1) the number of members of the tribunal is within the limits` 8
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 1(1) the number of members of the tribunal is within the limits` 3
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 1(1) the number of members of the tribunal is within the limits` 9
